  "description": "HITLIJ crystallizes in the hexagonal crystal system with space group P 63. Reported CIF formula moiety: C78 H124 Cl6 Gd3 N6 O13 Zn3 1-,3(C6 H16 N1 1+),3(C2 H6 O1),Cl4 Zn1 2-,0.5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 2 O neighbors; Gd1B (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Zn1B (Zn) has 2 O neighbors; Gd1D (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Zn1D (Zn) has 2 O neighbors; Zn2 (Zn) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.476-3.836 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.41-114.90°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C102H191Cl10Gd3N9O16.5Zn4.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
